From f0148e0000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH 0148e] evergo: mirror the early bootstrap console into SWEETLOG

read_sweetlog.py pulls the 4 MiB kernel console ring from the end of
userdata, but `sweet_early_panic()` (patch 0010) formats its text with
`sweet_early_putc()`, which draws straight to the bootstrap framebuffer and
never goes through `_cnputs` -> `sweet_log_append()`.  So a panic that
happens after journal replay is visible on the screen but ABSENT from
sweetlog.txt, which made several rounds of analysis conclude (wrongly)
that "the ring contains no panic, therefore the kernel never panicked".

`sweet_log_append()` only writes into a static in-memory ring with an
atomic counter: no locks, no allocation, no UFS dependency.  It is safe to
call at any bootstrap stage, including from panic() before a current thread
exists.  Feed it every character that sweet_early_putc() receives, before
any row/column processing, so the disk ring and the screen show the same
early text (including the panic header and its formatted arguments).

This is observation-only: no change to what panic() prints or to the
boot flow.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/sweet_early.c b/osfmk/arm64/sweet_early.c
index 45d6cb4..590aee5 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm64/sweet_early.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/sweet_early.c
@@ -28,6 +28,9 @@ extern unsigned char iso_font[256 * 16];
 static unsigned int early_row, early_col;
 static unsigned int early_started, early_disabled, early_panicking;
 
+/* bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c: writes into a static in-memory console ring. */
+extern void sweet_log_append(const char *c, int size);
+
 static void
 sweet_early_clear_row(void)
 {
@@ -42,6 +45,13 @@ sweet_early_clear_row(void)
 void
 sweet_early_putc(char c)
 {
+	/*
+	 * evergo (0148e): mirror every early character into the SWEETLOG ring
+	 * so read_sweetlog.py can see panics that happen before the normal
+	 * console path is up.  Safe here: sweet_log_append() is lock-free and
+	 * touches only a static ring.
+	 */
+	sweet_log_append(&c, 1);
 	if (early_disabled) {
 		return;
 	}
